NAME
    tree - list a directory as an indented tree

SYNOPSIS
    tree [path]

DESCRIPTION
    Recursively lists <path> (default: the current directory) as an indented
    tree, sorted by name, ending with an "N directories, M files" summary.
    ASCII branches (the console font is ASCII-only). . and .. are skipped.

    A path holds at most 16 names, and tree goes at most 16 levels down. A
    directory beyond either is listed and not looked into, and the line
    under it says so: "(not descended: path too long)" or "(not descended:
    deeper than tree goes)".

SEE ALSO
    ls
